    "updated_at": "2020-10-23T19:27:13Z",
    "body": "There are two problems here. Here's a reference to the [zsh-wrapper script](https://github.com/starship/starship/blob/master/src/init/starship.zsh#L47-L60) that is actually sourced when `eval \"$(starship init zsh)\"` is run.\r\n\r\n1. We are overriding `zle-keymap-select` [here](https://github.com/starship/starship/blob/master/src/init/starship.zsh#L56-L60) same as your snippet. Whichever is sourced second will have its behaviour executed. We need to make a fix in starship to decorate any existing `zle-keymap-select` widget that already exists. Your snippet should do the same.\r\n1. Starship [safely adds itself to the precmd hook](https://github.com/starship/starship/blob/master/src/init/starship.zsh#L44-L54) so that anything defined before it is still preserved while your snippet overrides it. If Starship runs first, it won't work at all. If starship runs after your snippet, it should work fine.",
